"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Walton County has come in under 90% of normal in October to November 37 times in 75 years, the most of any pair. That pair is also the driest, with a normal of 7.20 inches, and it came in at 53% of normal in 2025. This year so far the middle ran 27% of normal in March to April 2026 and 218% in May to June 2026. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grids 12475, 12775 and 13075 at 51% that year.</p>"}
